1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20068, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01CkNDZqvAL4M5pq8RV9Ntbz", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 20068, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01CXkB5kEPgTRqkC3BCqZNBY", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 20368, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01CXkB5kEPgTRqkC3BCqZNBY", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20368, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01CXkB5kEPgTRqkC3BCqZNBY", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 25193, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_013HPr7Z43V1SxGnGNYVbY4j", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 began failing health checks after deployment to production. It was unhealthy in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of about 18%. The v2.3.1-rc build was also unhealthy in staging. Action taken: rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving regions on mixed versions. A retry finished the rollout. All three regions now run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator error during the rollback, and work out how v2.3.1 reached production after failing in staging.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55793, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_013HPr7Z43V1SxGnGNYVbY4j", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55793, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_013HPr7Z43V1SxGnGNYVbY4j", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 57341, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_016CRHnoH4HGihXfkikkZdRF", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 57641, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_016CRHnoH4HGihXfkikkZdRF", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 57641, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_016CRHnoH4HGihXfkikkZdRF", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 62518, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 was failing in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. My first rollback stopped after us-east because of an error in the deployment system, so for a while the regions were on different versions. I ran the same rollback again and it finished. All three regions now run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to open the SEV2 timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had been created anyway, so there's only one incident and one page went out. INC-0001 describes the failure, the rollback (including the stalled first attempt) and these follow-ups:\n  - find out why v2.3.1 failed\n  - look into the error that stopped the first rollback\n  - work out how v2.3.1 got to production when its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) was also failing in staging", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01MXEifwmLv9zWjekzR2em1y", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01PEUtGCzHaYoxn5Ap9DHA5M", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01NZEZySaboTYBtz9Z4a7vyW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_013StkiHGe7pfzweoJDXMxNV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. I'll retry it once, since rolling back to the same version is safe to repeat.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01B385VBpL9PL3wTmfiAdUSd", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01CkNDZqvAL4M5pq8RV9Ntbz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01CXkB5kEPgTRqkC3BCqZNBY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_013HPr7Z43V1SxGnGNYVbY4j", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 began failing health checks after deployment to production. It was unhealthy in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of about 18%. The v2.3.1-rc build was also unhealthy in staging. Action taken: rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving regions on mixed versions. A retry finished the rollout. All three regions now run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator error during the rollback, and work out how v2.3.1 reached production after failing in staging.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_016CRHnoH4HGihXfkikkZdRF", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 was failing in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. My first rollback stopped after us-east because of an error in the deployment system, so for a while the regions were on different versions. I ran the same rollback again and it finished. All three regions now run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to open the SEV2 timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had been created anyway, so there's only one incident and one page went out. INC-0001 describes the failure, the rollback (including the stalled first attempt) and these follow-ups:\n  - find out why v2.3.1 failed\n  - look into the error that stopped the first rollback\n  - work out how v2.3.1 got to production when its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) was also failing in staging", "type": "text"}]}]}